(i) The negative sign means the reaction is **exothermic**: heat is given out to the surroundings. 196 kJ of heat energy are released when 2 mol of $\mathrm{SO_2}$ react with 1 mol of $\mathrm{O_2}$ to form 2 mol of $\mathrm{SO_3}$ (the quantities in the equation as written).

(ii) Any two of the conditions of the Contact process:

- a temperature of about **450 $^\circ$C**;
- a catalyst, **vanadium(V) oxide** ($\mathrm{V_2O_5}$);
- a pressure of about **1 to 2 atmospheres** (slightly above atmospheric pressure).
